<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-Trygg-Hansa H1 profit up 42 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Trygg-Hansa H1 profit up 42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurer Trygg-Hansa on</p>
<p>Tuesday posted its results for the six months ending June 30,</p>
<p>1997.</p>
<p>(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax result			    2,126 vs  1,494</p>
<p> Total result				1,996 vs  1,394</p>
<p>     non-life				  170 vs    367</p>
<p>     life and savings			163 vs     25</p>
<p>     other operations		    1,663 vs  1,002</p>
<p> Shareholder funds/shr (SKR) June 30   137 vs     99</p>
<p> Total shareholders funds	     11,337 vs  8,180</p>
<p> Gross premiums written		  6,442 vs  5,984</p>
<p>     non-life				3,150 vs  3,379</p>
<p>     life and savings			737 vs    390</p>
<p>    commissioned ops Trygg-Hansa Liv 2,555 vs  2,215</p>
<p> Trygg-Banken, deposits		  3,678 vs    939</p>
<p>		  lending		    8,144 vs  7,873</p>
<p>Trygg Funds, assets under</p>
<p>     management			    8,256 vs  4,776</p>
<p>NOTE --  A Reuters poll found the insurer was expected to post a pre-tax profit of 1.94 billion crowns in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
